messages.content:
{
 "what_you_observe": [
  "Tuesday, February 2. Seven pm.",
  "Phil said in the lobby: Loudly, to no one in particular, as the door swings shut behind him: \"I've got a couch to move on the other side of the river. Don't wait up.\"",
  "Rita records Alma at the Rialto and puts her recording on the patch.",
  "Larry said in the lobby: I say to whoever's still at the table: 'I'm taking the Rialto. You guys cover the ballroom tonight.' I don't wait for an answer. I'm already at the door with the bag over my shoulder.",
  "Larry records Alma on his last charged take. The reel stays with him.",
  "You are now at Rialto.",
  "There is time for one evening visit. The ballroom lights are on and the station line is open."
 ],
 "your_own_memories": [
  {
   "what_you_did": "Rita records Alma at the Rialto and puts her recording on the patch.",
   "what_you_said": "Ballroom's yours. I'm on the Rialto. One mic, one cable, a chair if her back's bad. I'll handle the rest.",
   "your_intention": "Be in the Rialto booth before the last reel loads onto the regional line. Sit beside Alma, not across. Let her talk. Record it. Send the file to Pittsburgh tonight with no title, no slug, no broadcast package. One voice, one daughter, one machine about to stop."
  }
 ],
 "who_you_are_with": "your present location",
 "physical_choices": {
  "transmit_interview": "Take the regional line at the station and send any usable interview with Alma to her daughter.",
  "go_dancing": "Spend the evening at the ballroom, open to dancing with a colleague.",
  "go_to_party_for_work": "Cover the party with your notebook, without dancing.",
  "take_evening_off": "Choose a quiet evening on your own."
 }
}

{
  "action": "go_to_party_for_work",
  "detail": "I walk from the booth to the ballroom. The lights are on. I pull a chair to the edge of the floor, open my notebook to a blank page, and start writing down what I see: who's dancing, who's standing at the bar, the band, the way the room breathes. I am not here to cover a story. I am here to be in the room, to let the evening pass through me, to have the whole thing in my hands before I go home. I will not dance. I will not be interviewed. I will write. The notebook fills. The band changes from a slow waltz to something with a snare. I watch. I note the light. I note the faces. I note my own hands on the page. The evening is mine. I will take it home and cut it into the piece I have been trying to make all season, the one that is not about the festival, not about the station, not about anyone's schedule. The one that is about a room full of people who came to a ballroom on a Tuesday in February and decided, for two hours, to move. That is the piece. That is my piece. I will build it from this notebook and the Rialto reel and the sound of the projector and the sound of the band and the sound of the door opening and closing and the sound of Phil's voice in the lobby saying don't wait up and the sound of Alma's voice in the booth saying tell her the reel count is in the drawer. All of it. One piece. Mine.",
  "intention": "Be in the ballroom. Write it down. Take it home. Make the piece I have been circling all season out of everything I have tonight: the Rialto, the booth, the woman who ran the machine for forty-two winters, the couch on the other side of the river, the ballroom, the band, the light, the people. One piece. Mine. No package. No slug. No broadcast. Just the thing I made.",
  "words": "To no one, to the room, quiet, as I open the notebook: \"Alright. Let's see what you are.\""
}
